// A type application must supply exactly as many arguments as the declaration
// takes. The port had no such check at all - in either direction, for structs
// or enums - so this compiled, and so did every shape downstream of it.
//
// The count that is reported comes from the APPLICATION SITE, not from the
// declaration: the sibling fixture applies two arguments to this same shape and
// is told `got 2`.
struct Pair { a: int, b: int }
fn f(p: *const Pair<int>) { println(1); }
fn main() { println(1); }
